      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Game-world design would be quite a bit easier if there was some sort of world toggle for this! As-is, there's not really any way I can see to have good-looking particle collisions with players, since only the player who was hit will see the collisions accurately. If you're trying to design, e.g., a gun that works with particle systems, then the player who's actually *firing* the weapon sees it pass right through the player they hit.\n\nI totally get not wanting to disrupt existing worlds that rely on this behavior, but I really wish there was an opt-in of some sort to get matching colliders for local vs. remote!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
